\newlabel{fig:teaser}{{1}{2}{Stage-3 feature trajectories of a weight-tied ConvNeXt (left; $9R$ applications of the shared block with $R{=}100$, $\Delta t{=}0.09$) and a standard ConvNeXt-T (right; each of nine blocks applied $R{=}100$ times with $\Delta t{=}0.01$), both integrated with Euler up to horizon $T{=}9$ (massive channel removed; $200$ ImageNet validation images, $20$ from each of $10$ classes). \textbf {Top:} states are flattened and mapped to $2048$ dimensions with a fixed Gaussian random projection \citep {johnson1984extensions,dasgupta2003elementary}, and PCA is fitted on all projected states of each model \citep {halko2011finding}; paths coloured by depth $t$, white dots mark integer $t$. \textbf {Bottom:} residual speed $\|f(x(t))\|$ (mean over images; shade: P10--P90). One shared block is a single autonomous field $\dot x = f(x)$; nine independent blocks switch the field at every integer, $\dot x = f_{\lfloor t\rfloor }(x)$}{figure.caption.1}{}}
