\newlabel{fig:kinematics-compare}{{3}{6}{Stage-3 kinematics over $T{=}9$ ($R{=}100$, Euler $\Delta t{=}0.01$; massive channel removed; mean and P5--P95 over $N{=}500$). \textbf {Top:} weight-tied ConvNeXt. \textbf {Bottom:} untied ConvNeXt-T. Columns: speed $\|v\|$, angular velocity $\omega $, acceleration $(\|a\|,a_t,a_n)$, curvature $\kappa {=}a_n/\|v\|^2$. On the untied row, pairs of micro-steps that straddle a block boundary are omitted from $\omega $, $a$ and $\kappa $: there $v$ is discontinuous and finite differences diverge as $\Delta t\!\to \!0$}{figure.caption.4}{}}
