\newlabel{fig:block-evals}{{6}{8}{ImageNet top-1 against the number of stage-3 block evaluations (Euler counts $1$ per step), without retraining. Purple solid: native tied prefixes ($k{=}1{\ldots }9$). Blue solid: native untied prefixes. Blue dashed: selected untied subsequences from App.~\ref {app:block-ops}. Blue dotted: equispaced untied subsets $\mathrm {round}(\mathrm {linspace}(0,8,L))$ with $\Delta t{=}9/L$ (\cref {tab:app-equispaced}). Purple dotted: coarse Euler of the tied stage at $T{=}9$ (App.~\ref {app:solvers}). Horizontal lines: full-depth accuracy of each model. The tied stage dominates at few evaluations through its prefixes; the untied stage wins at nine; coarse Euler of the tied stage is not the way to save compute}{figure.caption.9}{}}
